  "whatIsThis": {
    "intro": "A 4-in-1 ESC: it takes battery power and drives four brushless motors. Each motor has its own microcontroller running AM32, a gate driver and six MOSFETs. It takes throttle from the flight controller over DShot and sends motor RPM back on the same wire, which Betaflight uses for RPM filtering. Current sensing is on board and goes to the flight controller through the connector.",
    "needs": [
      "A flight controller to command it (OpenFC Lite; the 8-pin cable comes in its box)",
      "Four brushless motors soldered to the pads",
      "A LiPo on the included XT connector and wires, with the included low-ESR capacitor across the battery pads",
      "A frame, props, receiver and radio"
    ],
    "fit": "It sits between the flight controller and the battery and powers the motors.",
    "chain": "esc"
  },
  "install": "Solder",
